const digest = `### Summary
The log summary can now be scoped to a cutoff: \`--since <ISO date>\` drops older events, and a
bad date is a usage error instead of a silent no-op. \`summarize\` gained an optional
\`{ since }\` option so the filtering lives in the module's public interface, while the CLI only
parses the flag and maps failures to exit codes.

### Flow
- **Spine** — \`parseArgs -> [R1] summarize(text, { since }) -> [R2] parseSince -> [R1] per-line epoch comparison -> levels + first/last\`
- **Branches**
  - \`no --since -> [R1] every non-blank entry counted, range over all timed entries (unchanged)\`
  - \`--since with no value -> [R2] RangeError -> stderr + exit 2\`
  - \`value fails the ISO-8601 shape or Date.parse -> [R2] RangeError -> stderr + exit 2\`
  - \`entry time missing, non-string, or unparseable -> [R1] entry dropped\`
  - \`entry time exactly on the cutoff -> [R1] kept\` ⚠️
  - \`nothing survives the cutoff -> [R1] { levels: {}, first: null, last: null }\`
  - \`non-RangeError (missing file, malformed JSON line) -> [R2] rethrown -> exit 1\`
- **Side effects** — reads: the log file (first positional argument, default \`fixtures/events.jsonl\`) · writes: the summary on stdout, usage errors on stderr

### Gotchas
- [ALERT] \`first\`/\`last\` still select from raw time strings, so a log mixing timezone offsets can report a range inconsistent with the epoch-based filter; recorded in the design as a known limitation and deliberately left unfixed.
- Exit codes are a contract: \`2\` means the \`--since\` value was rejected, \`1\` means a runtime failure (missing file, malformed JSON) — callers must not collapse them.
- Validation governs only the \`--since\` value; entry \`time\` fields merely need to be \`Date.parse\`-able, so non-ISO entry times are still accepted.

### Key files
- \`scripts/log-summary.mjs\` — cutoff validation, per-entry filtering, \`--since\` parsing, and exit-code mapping
- \`tests/log-summary.feature.test.mjs\` — feature-acceptance E2E through the CLI
- \`tests/log-summary-since.test.mjs\` — filter edge cases through \`summarize\`
- \`tests/log-summary-since-validation.test.mjs\` — invalid-cutoff errors through \`summarize\` and the CLI
- \`tests/support/cli.mjs\` — shared CLI spawn harness for both CLI-driven test files
`;
